# Branch Feature: Cookie Module

## Score
- 0

## Intent
Track notable good and bad assistant behaviors with lightweight, durable feedback entries so the project can reinforce preferred patterns over time.

## Directives
- Feedback event types:
  - `cookie` = notably good behavior/code quality worth reinforcing.
  - `zuchinii` = notably bad behavior that should be corrected.
- The alternate spelling `zucchini` should be treated as equivalent to `zuchinii`.
- Log every awarded `cookie` or `zuchinii` in `.harbormaster/feedback/cookie_log.md`.
- Each log entry must be append-only and include:
  - date (`YYYY-MM-DD`)
  - type (`cookie` or `zuchinii`)
  - short reason (one line)
  - optional context (file/workflow reference)
- Keep reasons concise and behavior-focused so they are useful as future training signals.

## Logging format
- `- YYYY-MM-DD | type=<cookie|zuchinii> | reason=<brief reason> | context=<optional>`

## Current project application
- Cookie/zuchinii tracking is enabled for this project.
- Initial branch score is `0` (first creation in this project lineage).
